[{"source": "architecture", "severity": "note", "category": "golden-churn", "title": "Per-tick catalog_hash fold makes every behavior-neutral catalog change a whole-file T1 re-bless of all manifests", "location": "core/serialize.odin:111 (state_writer) vs harness/manifest.odin:117 + harness/run.odin:700", "evidence": "core/serialize.odin:111: \"w_u64(&w, state.catalog_hash)\" (inside state_writer, whose bytes are FNV-1a-64'd into every per-tick T1 hash); harness/manifest.odin:117: \"if m.catalog_hash != catalog_hash { append(fails, fmt.tprintf(\"T1: catalog drift — manifest %016x vs current %016x (re-bless deliberately)\", m.catalog_hash, catalog_hash)) ok = false }\"; harness/run.odin:700: \"if header.catalog_hash != cat.hash { append(fails, fmt.tprintf(\"replay: catalog drift — log %016x vs current %016x (defined rejection, ODN-11)\", header.catalog_hash, cat.hash)) return out, false }\"; this diff: audio.t1 @@ -3,1405 +3,1405 @@ with all 1400 per-tick hashes changed while audio.log.bin differs from its parent at exactly bytes 17..24 only (the 8-byte catalog_hash field; 608805064a32c466 -> 7bb80f94b1790625, the little-endian forms of 66c4324a06058860 -> 250679b1940fb87b).", "detail": "catalog_hash is bound twice: in the manifest header/check_manifest and the replay gate, AND folded into every per-tick state hash. The header checks alone already force a defined re-bless on any catalog retune; the per-tick fold adds nothing to the gate while rewriting all 1400 lines of audio.t1 (and every other .t1) for a behavior-neutral fold, making re-bless diffs opaque noise.", "recommended_fix": "Deliberate ODN-11 design ('the golden-stability rule') — acceptable, but consider header-only binding (drop state_writer's catalog_hash fold) so fold-only re-blesses become 1-line header diffs; document the change in the architecture before adopting."}]
